Maintain a current stack/string.
Recursively add ( and ).
Don't allow invalid parenthesis states.
Stop when all parentheses are used.
Copy the current state into res.
Backtrack using pop().

at every level we basically prune this problem and use right conditions
we start open and close from 0 and base case is when both equals n thats when all combo are xplored according to our conditions

two choices are if o < n then we can append open paranthesis freely 

and if c < o that means o are used more and we have options to explore on c as well

we use stack.pop after every dfs call so all options are explored


```python
class Solution:
    def generateParenthesis(self, n: int) -> List[str]:
        

        #stack = [] ; o = 0 c = 0 is is basically same, we dont decrease instead we increase
        stack = []
        res = []

        def dfs(o,c):

            if o == c == n:
                res.append("".join(stack))
            
            if o < n:
                stack.append('(')
                dfs(o+1,c)
                stack.pop()
            if c < o: #means opens are used more
                stack.append(')')
                dfs(o,c+1)
                stack.pop()

        dfs(0,0)
        
        return res

            
            
